      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Anticoagulation during percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) requires the monitoring of activated clotting time (ACT) to protect from periprocedural ischemic and bleeding complications; however, the optimal ACT values have not been established when PCI is performed with bivalirudin. After 495 consecutive patients treated for coronary artery disease with PCI received bivalirudin as a single anticoagulation agent, it was found that ACT is reproducible when bivalirudin is used during PCI and does not correlate with clinical events."},
